\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+13{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +13) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +13=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +13 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +9)-9+13 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda -3 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =3\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{3x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355408 #edb/ref 1080 "y={e}^{2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355408 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355408 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5391bd40-9dfe-5f5a-9861-a1093409b31b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355657 #edb/ref 1080 "y={e}^{4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355657 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355657 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "70773ae9-a152-5cc4-ac15-a00c4a6fe1f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355850 #edb/ref 1080 "y={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355850 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355850 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8638cc2f-34bc-5d19-b9c9-a973bfd6b17b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356173 #edb/ref 1080 "y={e}^{-4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356173 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356173 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "